sourceIssues.correction:
For g ≥ 2, GSp_{2g}(ℤ_p) permutes transitively only the 2^g sets Fl_J whose J contains exactly one of i and g+i for each i ≤ g, i.e. whose coordinate g-plane is Lagrangian for ψ; the Weyl group already does this. These Fl_J cover Fl.

Theorem 3.3.18(i) should be stated for these J only, and so should its consequences Theorem 4.1.1(i) and Lemma 4.3.3. For the other J, the proof does not show that 𝒱_J is affinoid perfectoid. The later uses need only a cover:
- Lemma 3.3.9;
- the existence of the perfectoid 𝒳*_{Γ(p^∞)};
- the Čech cover by the 𝒱_i in the proof of Theorem 4.3.1.
The Lagrangian 𝒱_J provide that cover.
